<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About HomeBillCuts — bill-first US home energy efficiency guides and product shortlists."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About HomeBillCuts</h1>
    <p>
      <!-- EDIT THIS BIO -->
      HomeBillCuts is a practical resource for US homeowners and renters who want to understand —
      and responsibly reduce — home energy use. We start with the bill, then work backward to
      habits, diagnostics, and only then equipment upgrades.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our tone is intentionally boring-honest: we avoid miracle claims, fake testimonials, and
      invented dollar-savings guarantees. Every home is different. Utility rates, climate zones,
      insulation, HVAC condition, and occupancy patterns matter more than any single product.
    </p>
    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Priority checklists you can act on this month</li>
      <li>Buyer’s guides that compare tradeoffs, not hype</li>
      <li>Clear affiliate disclosures when we recommend products</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Questions or corrections? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>. For how we handle affiliate
      relationships, read the <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
